1
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,000
The closer the entrance is to the palace,

2
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,000
the closer the exit will be
to the throne room over here.

3
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Well, okay. Then we're all in agreement.

4
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,000
We'll charge in as close as we can
from the exit by the central staircase.

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:36,000
[opening theme music playing]

6
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

7
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

8
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:17,000
[singer singing in English]

9
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:21,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

10
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Nobody told me the stronger the ability,
the bigger my stomach would get.

11
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:25,000
This was a mistake.

12
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:31,000
For a girl, there's nothing worse
than losing your figure.

13
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:35,000
I should go and ask Sir Leol
for a larger reward.

14
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:36,000
Right, Shidore?

15
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,000
[Hina] I keep her around
'cause she's a rare peon

16
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,000
that understands speech, but…

17
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,000
Come on. Can't you at least participate
in the conversation?

18
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,000
She's a foreigner.

19
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:58,000
She can't blend in
with the other citizens.

20
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:34,000
What? Is one escaped woman
really that important?

21
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:35,000
[whimpers]

22
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:37,000
[chuckles]

23
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:39,000
I can go find her for you.

24
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:52,000
The Royal Guard appreciates your work,
and I respect you too.

25
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:57,000
This could benefit both of us,
so what do you say we work together?

26
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:02,000
Excellent point.
You wait here while I go find something.

27
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,000
If he took his shoes off

28
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:33,000
and left them here
to avoid leaving footprints,

29
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:48,000
That was the day Taragette went missing.

30
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:52,000
If I had to bet,
I'd say that intruder killed him.

31
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:57,000
But that would mean that
after he left his shoes behind,

32
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:59,000
he disposed of Taragette's body.

33
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:20,000
No. I'll just catch the intruder myself.

34
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:28,000
I see.

35
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:31,000
The tracks lead deeper inside the palace.

36
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:33,000
This trumps Bizeff's woman.

37
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:35,000
Now, follow me!

38
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:01,000
I asked his name, but he didn't tell me.

39
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,000
[wind blowing]

40
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:21,000
[King] Well, who am I?

41
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:25,000
A nameless king in a borrowed castle.

42
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:43,000
I fear nothing
except the tedium that it will bring!

43
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:10,000
[giggles] And with that,
he's beaten all of us.

44
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:29,000
Then it's up to you to tell him that.
There is no way I'm gonna get hit again.

45
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:33,000
[Neferpitou] How does this
sound to you, sire?

46
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:36,000
We can block all the aura
in the vicinity surrounding you.

47
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:39,000
It is my fervent hope
that it would prevent

48
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,000
my mere presence from bothering you.

49
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:44,000
[King] You suggest
that I stay in one place?

50
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:47,000
Or could you simply move the area?

51
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:50,000
Could its location change
as I moved around freely?

52
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:51,000
Is it possible?

53
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:55,000
I refuse to have my movement
constantly monitored.

54
00:07:56,000 --> 00:08:00,000
No. We would never propose to you
something so restrictive.

55
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:03,000
[King] So if I do not wish
to endure your presence,

56
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:07,000
I will only be able to move
within that confined area?

57
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:13,000
Then if it were my wish to go elsewhere,
you would have to move it. Is that right?

58
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:22,000
at least until tomorrow's sorting.

59
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,000
That will suffice.

60
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:26,000
It's not enough?

61
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:43,000
that your En is as worthless
as a common sieve. Am I wrong?

62
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:50,000
would limit its benefits.

63
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:53,000
I would miss any attacks
coming from underground.

64
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:03,000
[King] Are you referring to Komugi, then?

65
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:07,000
No. I am referring to the 11 soldiers

66
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:10,000
who still remain stationed
within the palace.

67
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:14,000
They have all been allowed the freedom
to come and go from here as they see fit,

68
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:15,000
with minimal supervision.

69
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:19,000
And of course we check thoroughly
every time one of them enters,

70
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:23,000
but if a soldier were to be
somehow controlled by the enemy,

71
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:26,000
it would be difficult at best
to know for sure. Also--

72
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:48,000
You will not come unless summoned,
so disturb me at your own peril.

73
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:56,000
on or above the second floor anyway.

74
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:07,000
If intruders come up from underground,

75
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:09,000
you will be in a good position
to deal with them.

76
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:13,000
Still, the King's been
in a real bad mood lately.

77
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:28,000
would be more than enough
to remove all doubt.

78
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:34,000
However, that would be
a grave insult to the King.

79
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:37,000
No, I'm only making excuses.

80
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:45,000
Whatever is growing within him

81
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:49,000
is causing me
unbearable anxiety and dread.

82
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,000
I can't bear it.

83
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:02,000
[Welfin] Damn. Looks like
the rain washed away the trail,

84
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:05,000
but now I have the answer.

85
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:08,000
The intruder hid here
to check the second floor,

86
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:12,000
but instead of going upstairs,
he left the palace.

87
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:29,000
the King will definitely kill you.

88
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:32,000
Go and let everyone else know that too.

89
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:34,000
Sir!

90
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:38,000
Wings. What if the intruder
has the ability to fly?

91
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:42,000
The shoes and the scent
may have been a diversion.

92
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:45,000
It's possible that he flew up
to the second floor.

93
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:47,000
-Sir Youpi.
-Hmm?

94
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:49,000
Oh, uh…

95
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:52,000
Pitou is monitoring the palace with En.

96
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:56,000
If they'd made it up to the second floor,
they would have been caught.

97
00:11:56,000 --> 00:12:00,000
-[chuckles] No. Sorry. It was nothing.
-Hmm?

98
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:04,000
[Welfin] But that doesn't make sense.
How did the intruder reach the stairway?

99
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Sir Youpi…

100
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:08,000
[Menthuthuyoupi] Yeah? What is it?

101
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:11,000
Has there ever been a time
that Sir Pitou stopped using En?

102
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:15,000
I mean, what about that day last week
when it rained?

103
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:18,000
Wait. What?
You didn't hear about what happened?

104
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:23,000
There was a massive panic right after
the King tore off his own left arm.

105
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:24,000
Huh?

106
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,000
Pouf was in charge of En

107
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:29,000
while Pitou was responsible
for healing him.

108
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:32,000
[Welfin] And how wide is Pouf's En,
if you don't mind me asking?

109
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:34,000
And how the hell would I know that?

110
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:36,000
As wide as Pitou's?

111
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:47,000
It all makes sense.

112
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:50,000
The question now is
what the intruder's objective was

113
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:53,000
and whether he's still
hiding around here somewhere.

114
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:00,000
[yawns]

115
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,000
[Welfin] I should report to Pitou or Pouf.

116
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:03,000
Pouf would be best.

117
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:09,000
And, if possible, I need to determine
exactly what the intruder's objective was.

118
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:12,000
Otherwise, my report would be

119
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:15,000
that the intruder
somehow made it inside the palace,

120
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:24,000
I guess I can make up an objective,

121
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:27,000
but if the intruder is captured,
they'll find out I lied for sure.

122
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:31,000
But then if I tell the Royal Guard
about my suspicion

123
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:43,000
I have an idea.

124
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:48,000
So the intruder captured one of my men.

125
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:52,000
Leol tells me
that this intruder is able to teleport.

126
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:55,000
He may be working with your woman,

127
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,000
and they might have
teleported out together.

128
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:07,000
But I was able to discern their objective.

129
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:08,000
And?

130
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:12,000
They planned to blow up the palace.

131
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:13,000
Yeah, right.

132
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:15,000
[gasps] We must tell the Royal Guard!

133
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:17,000
-No.
-Huh?

134
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:21,000
What's the rush? We can tell them
right after you and I find the bomb.

135
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:23,000
But there's no time!

136
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:27,000
Just calm down
and think about it from their perspective.

137
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:31,000
If they want to blow up the palace,
then they'll wait until the King's here.

138
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:33,000
And when's that?

139
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:38,000
When all the citizens have been assembled,
before the ceremony begins.

140
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:45,000
It'll be a sight to behold.

141
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:55,000
It's safe to assume that
the enemy's reached the same conclusion.

142
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:56,000
[Bizeff] True.

143
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:20,000
The Royal Guard
should know that we're serious.

144
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:24,000
If we save the King's life,
they're bound to be grateful to us.

145
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:26,000
Right?

146
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:29,000
Yes, that's… that's true.

147
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:34,000
As soon as I find the bomb,
I'll contact you.

148
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:35,000
Yes, that's perfect.

149
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:38,000
[Welfin scoffs]

150
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:09,000
Hold on. About your ability…

151
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:18,000
and then I'll tap you
when I start to hold my breath again,

152
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:19,000
so don't you forget.

153
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:23,000
[laughs] Fine,
but there's no need to push your limits.

154
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:26,000
Give yourself all the buffer you need.

155
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:29,000
Just leave things to me
whenever God's Accomplice isn't active.

156
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:33,000
And you can trust me.
I know what I'm doing here. Hmm?

157
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:49,000
Tracking the smell of cigarette smoke
is really easy for them.

158
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:54,000
We could all be knocked out
the same second I take my first breath.

159
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:58,000
The boss will put up a smoke screen
when we go in. It'll be fine.

160
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:03,000
You may be right, but I still want
to eliminate as much risk as possible.

161
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:06,000
I don't want to do anything
I might regret.

162
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:17,000
and were discussing something.

163
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:20,000
Pitou stayed,
while Youpi went back inside.

164
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:25,000
As for Pouf, he returned to the air,
so I don't think anything has changed.

165
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:30,000
I'll let you know
if anything else happens.

166
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:44,000
[Gon] Oh.
So I guess he still has his doubts.

167
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:48,000
Well, I can pretty much guarantee
that they'll be near the King.

168
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:50,000
Hey, you don't know that.

169
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:52,000
We have to be ready for anything.

170
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:55,000
We don't wanna be caught off guard
if something happens.

171
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:58,000
[Ikalgo] If you knew how loyal they were,
you wouldn't say that.

172
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:01,000
I'm telling you there's no way
they'd ever leave the King.

173
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:04,000
The Royal Guard is always right there
by his side. You can count on it.

174
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:12,000
-[Ikalgo] Exceptions? Like what?
-[Killua] There are all kinds of things…

175
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:30,000
so maybe he's been making babies.

176
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:32,000
Yeah, I guess.

177
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:35,000
I hadn't thought of that,
but I guess it would give the King

178
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:38,000
a good reason to keep the Royal Guard
far away from his chamber.

179
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:40,000
You think what Bizeff was doing

180
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:04,000
[Knuckle] Glad we thought of this
before we set out.

181
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:06,000
[Shoot] If we hadn't been bracing for it,

182
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:09,000
we would have been
completely caught off guard.

183
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:10,000
Do you get it now?

184
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:13,000
I'm telling you,
you can never overthink something.

185
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:17,000
And there are lots of other things
we haven't even thought of yet.

186
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:18,000
[scoffs]

187
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:21,000
[Killua] Yeah,
something's still bothering me.

188
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:31,000
Right.

189
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:36,000
[Killua] It bothers me, but the existence
of a third party, woman or not,

190
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:37,000
is a good thing to consider.

191
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:49,000
Hold on a second.

192
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:52,000
I thought that was just a theory
you were thinking about.

193
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:56,000
Yeah, but you agreed that
there was no other logical explanation.

194
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:59,000
You realize you're contradicting yourself.

195
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:03,000
Didn't you just get through telling us
that there could be other exceptions?

196
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:04,000
Following that logic,

197
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:22,000
Yeah.

198
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:24,000
Right. Just think about it.

199
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:29,000
Why would anyone want to hurt themselves?
For what reason?

200
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:46,000
That does make sense.

201
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:51,000
That would mean we're not dealing
with an unemotional despot here,

202
00:20:56,000 --> 00:21:00,000
He's willing to endure searing pain
for the sake of his pride.

203
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:04,000
People like him
will never be willing to compromise.

204
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:07,000
I know that much from my own experience.

205
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:11,000
If the King won't budge,
then neither will his Guards,

206
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:15,000
so count on combat being our only option.

207
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:20,000
[Killua] Morel summed everything up nicely
but he's wrong.

208
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:25,000
The King's self-harm,
the existence of a third party…

209
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:29,000
We're still nowhere close to figuring out
what really happened.

210
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:34,000
I've got a feeling
that whatever the answer is,

211
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:37,000
it has the potential
to completely screw up our entire plan.

212
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:39,000
[Morel] It's time.

213
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:42,000
One minute left to go.

214
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:44,000
Gather round.

215
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:46,000
[Killua] Damn. We're out of time.

216
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:53,000
[exhales]

217
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:04,000
Here we go.

218
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:09,000
-Get ready to rumble!
-[closing theme music playing]

219
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:11,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

220
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:28,000
[upbeat music playing]

221
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:33,000
[Gon] Next time, Charge and Invade.

222
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:35,000
Nothing beats having a hot pot in winter.

223
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:37,000
[Killua] Reminds me of mystery pots.

224
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:38,000
[Gon] Charge into the pot!
